{
	"$comment": "Merch print files only (no mockups). Trim sizes, bleed, safe areas and methods follow the spyglass-ds and context-ds engines (common vendor print areas; they are conventions, so confirm with the vendor template). Layouts are in inches from the trim. Words are drawn only when passed (the address is the brand's own); `sample` is drawn with --sample. Only the approved lockups (brand/assets/logo.json: the primary logo and the mark, in off-black, off-white or home-red as brand/logo ships them), the share-image themes and the illustration parts are used. Ground variants print a theme to the bleed; one-color variants are the logo and words alone in one brand color on a transparent ground (art needs more than one color, so it is left out of them, and what is left closes up: `flow` says from the top or round the middle, `fixed` parts stay; a part with `only: one` is drawn only in the one-color variants, where the art cannot be); color is the full-color art on a transparent ground for DTG. Documents (kind document: business card, letterhead, report cover, one-pager, case study, event badge, name tag, certificate) use the same engine; the brand has no stationery, so they are set only from its lockups, type, themes, hairlines and art. Their sizes are paper standards.",
